'''''Symphytum asperum''''' is a [[flowering plant]] of the genus ''[[Symphytum]]'' in the family [[Boraginaceae]]. Common names include '''rough comfrey'''<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |access-date=2014-10-17}}</ref> and '''prickly comfrey'''.<ref>{{PLANTS|id=SYAS|taxon=Symphytum asperum|accessdate=7 December 2015}}</ref> It is the tallest ''Symphytum'' species.<ref>{{cite book |last=Hills |first=Lawrence D. |title=Comfrey: Past, Present and Future |publisher=Faber & Faber |date=2011-10-20 |isbn=978-0-571-28091-9}}</ref> It is native to Asia, and it is known in Europe and North America as an [[introduced species]] and sometimes a [[weed]]. ''[[Symphytum × uplandicum]]'', the naturally occurring hybrid with the common comfrey (''[[Symphytum officinale]]''), is the economically most important kind of comfrey.

